==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Grudge Cat''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Ritual Cat''' when obtained from the [[Salaryman Awakes!]] (may be dropped on the first stage but guaranteed on the second stage) and is level 20 or above.

==Strategy/Usage==
Due to his low stats and high cost, Salaryman Cat is only viable in early-game stages as a general attacker and should not be used later on.

==='''True Form'''===
Ritual Cat is merely stronger, with better stats that make him worth using in a wider part of [[The Battle Cats]]. Sadly, this part of the game is already trivial compared to the stages where his True Form can be obtained in the first place. In other words, by the time you get him, he will be obsolete in 1-3-Crown stages due to low overall stats for his cost, recharge time and role overall.

However, there is one use for this cat: a 4-Crown alternative to [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]]. He gains use here as a cat with similar attack power, higher health, shorter deploy rate for no Slow ability, and higher cost. He shares many similarities with Can Can, with those above being the only major differences. His Strengthen can also work well considering his health at Lv.50 being 81000. That, combined with his low knockback count, makes this cat a strong pusher for 4-Crown stages, and a viable alternative to Can Can there.

