==Trivia==
*Prior to [[Version 15.7 Update|Version 15.7]], Salaryman Cat's descriptions read as follows:
<pre>Salaryman Cat
Let's not forget those who work hard everyday.
These people pay Worker Cat's salary. Its last
resort is an magnificent DoGeZa. Strong vs. Red</pre>
<pre>Grudge Cat
A Salaryman Cat who couldn't take the abuse
from his boss and resorted to Anti-Red
occultism. Curse them all! (Area Attack)</pre>
<pre>Ritual Cat
This world is too brutal and unfair to tolerate!
Primitive rage has overtaken him.  Why flame on
social media when you can flame IRL? (Area Atk)</pre>
**Salaryman Cat's original description had a typo. It said, "an magnificent DoGeZa", instead of "''a'' magnificent DoGeZa".
*The "DoGeZa" in Salamaryman Cat's description refers to how he ends his attack animation: the ''[http://yabai.com/p/3047 dogeza]'', a prostrating pose in which one kneels directly on the ground on hands and feet while bowing low enough for their head to touch the floor, expressing deep sorrow or gratitude to someone else. The ''dogeza'' was once a common element of Japanese etiquette used to show respect to nobles, but is now a rare sight outside of pop culture.
*Grudge Cat's outfit is based on what someone would wear during the practice of a cursing method named "[[wikipedia:Ushi no koku mairi|Ushi no koku mairi]]", where a nail is hammered into a doll, resulting in the death of a desired target. Although the ritual is usually performed with an iron crown holding the candles, Grudge Cat is using a simple headband to perform the curse.
*The "GoSuN" nail in Grudge Cat's Japanese description is named after the word ''gosun'' (五寸), meaning "five inches".
*The first line of Ritual Cat's Japanese description contains an almost-word-for-word reference to the full title of [[wikipedia:Takashi Sorimachi|Takashi Sorimachi]]'s 1998 hit single "[[wikipedia:ja:POISON 〜言いたい事も言えないこんな世の中は〜|POISON 〜Ītai Koto mo Ienai Konna Yo no Naka wa〜]]" (POISON 〜言いたい事も言えないこんな世の中は〜). The only parts missing are "poison" and the "wa" (は) at the end.
*The "BouGeN" post in Ritual Cat's Japanese description is named after the word ''bōgen'' (暴言), meaning a crass, reckless remark or outright abusive language.
*[[wikipedia:Labor Thanksgiving Day|Labor Thanksgiving Day]] is the Japanese national holiday mentioned in Salaryman Cat's Japanese description, and the holiday is the basis of the [[Loving Labour (Monthly Event)|Loving Labour]] event.
**This explains the typo in the [[Cat Guide]], stating that this unit is unlocked from "Loving Labor" instead of [[Loving Labour (Monthly Event)|Loving Labour]].
*The name of Ritual Cat's ability was revealed by the introduction of the "Filter" option in [[The Battle Cats|BCEN]] 3.5.0.
*[[Class Rep Cat (Special Cat)|Class Rep Cat]] is likely a younger version of him, based on his Normal Form's description.

